  "details": "Currently, the only way to unpose a physbone (besides grabbing it or using Release Poses) is to disable the physbone and re-enable it. This is a problem, because it causes the physbone to immediately snap back to its rest position, as opposed to doing it smoothly. \n\nIdeally, I would like to have animation logic be able to un-pose physbones. We already have the `IsPosed` parameter for physbones, so if a parameter driver could change that value, it would solve this problem entirely.",
